messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 317 and 222? Please reason step by step.. I think the correct answer is: 70174\n', '<think>.\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 317 and 222, I will follow these steps:.\n\n1. **Understand the multiplication**: We need to multiply 317 by 222. This means we are essentially adding 317 to itself 222 times or adding 222 to itself 317 times.\n\n2. **Set up the multiplication**: We can use the standard algorithm for multiplication. This involves multiplying each digit of the second number (222) by each digit of the first number (317) and then adding the results.\n\n3. **Break down the multiplication**:.\n   - First, multiply 317 by 200 (which is 222 without the last two digits):.\n     \\[.\n     317 \\times 200 = 317 \\times (2 \\times 100) = (317 \\times 2) \\times 100.\n     \\].\n     Calculate \\(317 \\times 2\\):.\n     \\[.\n     317 \\times 2 = 634.\n     \\].\n     Then multiply by 100:.\n     \\[.\n     634 \\times 100 = 63400.\n     \\].\n\n   - Next, multiply 317 by 20 (which is 222 without the last digit):.\n     \\[.\n     317 \\times 20 = 317 \\times (2 \\times 10) = (317 \\times 2) \\times 10.\n     \\].\n     We already know \\(317 \\times 2 = 634\\), so:.\n     \\[.\n     634 \\times 10 = 6340.\n     \\].\n\n   - Finally, multiply 317 by 2 (which is the last digit of 222):.\n     \\[.\n     317 \\times 2 = 634.\n     \\].\n\n4. **Add the results**:.\n   - Add the three products together:.\n     \\[.\n     63400 + 6340 + 634.\n     \\].\n\n5. **Perform the addition**:.\n   - First, add 63400 and 6340:.\n     \\[.\n     63400 + 6340 = 69740.\n     \\].\n   - Then add 634 to the result:.\n     \\[.\n     69740 + 634 = 70374.\n     \\]. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
